 the river to jabba  but it was the love of the character's  potential that inspired later star wars  writers to flesh him out in other  projects besides his iconic armor boba  fett also flies a very specific ship  which boasts a different design from  other ships in the star wars universe  and it also used to boast a very  specific name as well slave 1. though  the ship is never called slave one by  name in any of the live-action films the  designation was used in extended  universe projects like toys video games  comics and cartoons for decades however  in 2021 the new lego star wars  mandalorian sets came out and the ship  was just called boba fett's starship in  an interview with jedi news the lego  star wars designers said that the name  slave one quote it's just something that  disney doesn't want to use anymore of  course some fans were internet outraged  but by any name it's still a cool ship  boba fett's starship as a republic era  fire spray 31 class spacecraft  previously owned by fett's father jango  fett during the clone wars like fed's  portable armory of tools and weapons on  his person the starship is highly  customized and armed to the teeth with  both subtle and striking weaponry one of  the most unique features of the starship  is its ability to rotate on a gimbal  flying vertically in the air in space  while landing horizontally all while  keeping the pilot seat and cargo area  facing upright  there are many different languages in  star wars and a special code shared  between boba fett and his father jango  fett is one of them first identified as  a specific language in a 2019 video on  the star wars kids youtube channel  titled every language and star wars that  code is briefly heard in episode 2  attack of the clones when obi-wan kenobi  meets the two at their home on kamino  django speaks to his son infect code as  obi-wan questions a bounty hunter about  any recent trips to coruscant and his  feelings about the clone army created in  his imag